<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    x86 `rep movs`/`rep stos` as memcpy/memset (`option repstring on|off`,
    default on; stage P3, the late fullloop pass beside `strlenscan`).

    The fixtures (repstring.c beside them, gcc -Os, x86-64 and i386) copy and
    fill with the repeat-prefixed string instructions gcc inlines at -Os.
    SLEIGH lifts each as a loop inside the one instruction.

    The first pass of each image (`option repstring off`) shows those loops:
    `while (v3) { ... *a0 = *a1; v3 -= 1; ... }`. The second (the shipped
    default) prints one builtin call per instruction, with the byte count the
    element count times the element width, and a pointer read after the loop
    reads its final value (`copy_end` returns the destination plus the count).
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
